Z||000003||tomanyfieros||11-25-2001||03:08 PM||||i have heard (and i dont know if this is true or not) that they stopped them because the 89 prototype was going to beat the corvette (89 vette) and GM forced pontiac to stop the production, BUT if GM really made pontiac stop making them because they would beat the vette, why not change it to make it not beat the vette and keep making them? <BR>defines....<BR>*beat-faster, better looking, ect. <BR>Thanx Jason<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||11-25-2001||04:16 PM||||Lets face it a two seater car is a limited market auto whether it is sold as a commuter car or as a sports car.  In 1984 136,000 Fieros were sold,in 1985 76,000, 1986 84,000, 1987 46,500 and in 1988 26,000.  The market became saturated.  As people looked for a replacement car 4 or 5 years after the first purchase, GM had pulled the plug on the Fiero and gave us the Lemans as the commuter car. (Korean crap no less)<P>Rather than make a run of 30,000 car, GM sets a quota of 50,000, cuts the advertising budget and pulls any promotional programs for the Fiero and leaves the sales to the dealers who just want to sell the most expensive car you ca afford.  So Pontiac dealers sell the Firebird/Trans am to "sportcar" enthusists and ignore the Fiero.<P>The Fiero manufacturing process was great for making new styled cars without expensive retooling. New body panels of multiple syles would just bolt onto the space age frame.  Improvements to suspension and engines could easily be modified as could interior components making  "new" car every couple of years. Lots of potential.<P>Hence we get to buy rebody kits, do engine swaps, brake upgrades with all the complexity you can afford or just keep the car basically stock by replacing components.  Except for frame rust, the space age frame will last.  The body panels won't rust, but will break in an accident and can easily be replaced.<P>Th bean counters of the world rule.||||reg||1
Z||000005||BlackStang95||11-25-2001||04:19 PM||||It was cancelled due to declining sales...they were down from 140k in 84 to 25k in 88, the novelty wore off.||||reg||1
Z||000006||lou||11-25-2001||04:40 PM||||It is to your advantage that it was discontinued as it remains as one of the most original american cars ever built.  If they had kept making them they might just have become as common as .... well Mustangs!<BR>||||reg||1
