Z||000011||FieroHarry||11-25-2001||09:10 PM||||Capt Kirk,<P>Think about what your asking, the Fiero as old as it is and (depending on your mileage) has the same problems as any other car with similar issues.<P>Personally ive owned mine (im 3rd owner) for 4.5 years.<BR>We met when she had 167k miles and now she has 272k miles.<P>Ive done the following "repairs":<BR>water pump<BR>clutch<BR>brakes x2<BR>heater core<BR>1 head light motor repair<BR>fuel pump<BR>1 relay<BR>tie rods innner and outer<BR>ball joints<BR>control arm bushings<P>Thats not much at all for a car thats 17 years old and with 3 lifetimes under foot.<P>I love my car so much ive dropped at least $5000 in improvements alone.<P>I will stand up in any crowded place across this country and shout "I LOVE MY FIERO AND PONTIAC WAS STUPID FOR EVER STOPPING THEM"<P>Nuff said  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B>||||reg||14
